The port follows the released FEM, DDSP and DMTet algorithms. The clipping
tables in tables.py are copied from src/dmtet/geometry/dmtet_geometry.py,
with its NVIDIA copyright and proprietary-rights notice retained there.
The pinned repository has no top-level license. This notice records
provenance and does not grant additional rights to upstream material.

Author assets and source are archived locally by fetch.py, outside Git.
Reference fixtures are numerical outputs of the pinned author source with
CPU device placement and the dependency substitutions recorded in their
manifest. The port uses separately installed PyTorch, torchaudio, GeomLoss,
NumPy, SciPy, meshio, Open3D and Bempp-cl under their respective licenses.
